 slip, and it started a fight on the left side, where the rest of the game was played."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "C2 lost 22.5 points, taking Black from -16.0 to -38.5. The engine wanted F6, out in the open. By then White's D-column wall ran from D2 to D5, and Black chose to add stones to the cramped left side."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "C1 lost 28.2 points, from -39.0 to -67.2, and the engine preferred G5. Black's stones at B2, C2 and D1 were hemmed in along the bottom edge, and this move spent another turn there while the right side stayed open."}, {"turn": 33, "text": "A2 was the worst move of the game, losing 38.0 points and dropping Black from -47.5 to -85.5. The engine's choice was H6. It was one more move in the already cramped bottom-left corner, and Black never got back within 47 points."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "White's E8 lost 33.5 points, the 10k's biggest slip, lifting Black from -85.6 to -52.1; the engine preferred H4. Black held the right-hand side and stayed near -48 to -52 to the end, but a lead of about 50 points was too much to make up."}]}, "audit": null}